      "description": "The one filled control per region (Play, Pause, Resume): off-white slab, charcoal text, square corners.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-primary\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"14\" y=\"4\" width=\"4\" height=\"16\"/><rect x=\"6\" y=\"4\" width=\"4\" height=\"16\"/></svg>Pause</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-primary{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:36px;min-width:104px;padding:0 10px;border:0;border-radius:0;background:var(--primary);color:var(--primary-foreground);font:500 14px/1 \"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;cursor:pointer;transition:background .2s} .ds-btn-primary:hover{background:color-mix(in oklch,var(--primary) 80%,transparent)} .ds-btn-primary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Header Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-link",
      "description": "Lowercase words spread across the top; the wordmark centred as the home button; a square marks the current page.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><a class=\"ds-nav-link is-active\"><i></i>compare</a><a class=\"ds-nav-link\"><i></i>settings</a><a class=\"ds-wordmark\">intersection</a><a class=\"ds-nav-link\"><i></i>about</a><span class=\"ds-nav-link\"><i class=\"on\"></i>offline demo</span></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);align-items:center;padding:0 24px;height:60px;background:var(--background);font:450 16px/1.5 \"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.01em} .ds-nav>:nth-child(2),.ds-nav>:nth-child(4){justify-self:center} .ds-nav>:nth-child(3){justify-self:center} .ds-nav>:last-child{justify-self:end} .ds-nav-link{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;color:color-mix(in oklch,var(--foreground) 72%,transparent);text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer;transition:color .2s} .ds-nav-link i{width:6px;height:6px;background:var(--foreground);opacity:0;transition:opacity .2s} .ds-nav-link:hover{color:var(--foreground)} .ds-nav-link:hover i{opacity:.4} .ds-nav-link.is-active{color:var(--foreground)} .ds-nav-link.is-active i{opacity:1} .ds-nav-link i.on{opacity:1;background:var(--subtle-foreground)} .ds-wordmark{font-weight:640;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:-.035em;color:var(--foreground)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Controller Block",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "mode-action",
      "description": "One side of the choice on Home: display title, summary, a legend column of meaning squares and the run action. The whole block is the hit area.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-mode\"><h2>traditional</h2><p>A fixed timer, blind to traffic.</p><ol><li>30 s green, north/south<i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i></li><li>3 s yellow<i style=\"background:var(--signal-amber)\"></i></li><li>2 s all red<i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i></li><li class=\"faint\"><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i></li></ol><button>Run traditional <span>→</span></button></section>",
      "css": ".ds-mode{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:20px;text-align:right;color:var(--foreground);font-family:\"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;background:var(--background);padding:24px} .ds-mode h2{margin:0;font-size:48px;font-weight:620;line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.045em} .ds-mode p{margin:-12px 0 0;color:var(--muted-foreground);font-size:16px} .ds-mode ol{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;font-size:14px} .ds-mode li{display:flex;flex-direction:row-reverse;align-items:center;gap:12px} .ds-mode li.faint{opacity:.3} .ds-mode i{width:9px;height:9px} .ds-mode button{background:none;border:0;color:var(--foreground);font:560 18px/1.4 \"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.02em;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:transparent;text-underline-offset:.3em;transition:text-decoration-color .2s} .ds-mode button:hover{text-decoration-color:color-mix(in oklch,var(--foreground) 70%,transparent)} .ds-mode button span{display:inline-block;transition:transform .3s} .ds-mode button:hover span{transform:translateX(4px)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Provenance Mark",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "square-mark",
      "description": "Where a value came from, as a square and a word: hollow Mock, solid Live, steel Rule-based.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-prov mock\"><i></i>Mock</span> <span class=\"ds-prov live\"><i></i>Live</span> <span class=\"ds-prov rule\"><i></i>Rule-based</span>",
      "css": ".ds-prov{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-right:12px;font:500 12px/1 \"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif} .ds-prov i{width:7px;height:7px;background:currentColor} .ds-prov.mock{color:var(--muted-foreground)} .ds-prov.mock i{background:none;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px currentColor} .ds-prov.live{color:var(--foreground)} .ds-prov.rule{color:var(--safety)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Signal Lamps",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "square-mark",
      "description": "Each movement group's light as a square in the lamp colour, then its name, in tabular type.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-lamp\"><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i>N/S</span><span class=\"ds-lamp\"><i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i>E/W</span>",
      "css": ".ds-lamp{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-right:12px;color:var(--foreground);font:400 12px/1 \"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums} .ds-lamp i{width:10px;height:10px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Signal-timing Unit Chart",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "timeline-cell",
      "description": "Signal rows and participant rows as one square per time step on the simulation clock; empty steps stay visible as faint cells.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-grid\"><span>N/S light</span><div><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-green)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-amber)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-amber)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--signal-red)\"></i></div><span>Agent A</span><div><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--group-ns)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--group-ns)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--group-ns)\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i></div><span>JEV</span><div><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--jev)\"></i><i style=\"background:var(--jev)\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i><i class=\"e\"></i></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:84px auto;row-gap:3px;align-items:center;padding:16px;background:var(--panel);font:400 12px/1 \"Onest Variable\", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;color:var(--muted-foreground)} .ds-grid div{display:flex;gap:3px} .ds-grid i{width:10px;height:10px} .ds-grid i.e{background:var(--cell)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Unit Bar",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "legend-square",
      "description": "A probability or progress as twenty 9px squares, five percent each.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-unit\"><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"f\"></i><i class=\"\"></i><i class=\"\"></i><i class=\"\"></i><i class=\"\"></i><i class=\"\"></i><i class=\"\"></i></div>",
      "css": ".ds-unit{display:flex;gap:3px;padding:12px;background:var(--panel)} .ds-unit i{width:9px;height:9px;background:var(--cell)} .ds-unit i.f{background:var(--jev)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Both Sides of the Junction",
    "overview": "A warm charcoal room with one live scale model of an intersection in the middle of it. The two ways of running that intersection stand on either side of the model like the two camps of a data essay, each drawn as a column of small coloured squares that spells out its mechanism. Type sits directly on the ground: a wide, tight grotesk in warm off-white, lowercase in the navigation and the wordmark, with no bars, cards or pills around it. Colour lives only in squares, and every square means one thing.\n\nThe interface borrows two references and keeps them apart. The chrome takes its palette, type and lowercase restraint from a dark grotesk portfolio header: charcoal ground, off-white words spread across the top, nothing boxed. The data takes its form from a unit-chart essay: crisp squares in a few saturated colours, two millimetres apart, one square per unit. The 3D scene stays the brightest, most detailed thing on screen; the opening sequence earns that by showing one car alone before the world appears around it.\n\nDensity is moderate. Home is airy and presenter-friendly; the simulation is denser so it reads at laptop distance. Every visual decision is a token in `src/index.css`, and the 3D scene reads its `--scene-*` and semantic colours at runtime.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm charcoal room (hue 75, near-zero chroma) and warm off-white type; the scene's lamp is the only light.",
      "One family, Onest, from the poster-scale intro wordmark down to tabular readouts.",
      "Squares, not dots: crisp, unrounded, 7 to 12px, 2 to 3px apart, each a single meaning.",
      "No containers on the ground: titles, legends and links sit directly on the room. Only surfaces that float over the scene get a slab.",
      "Square corners everywhere (`--radius: 0`).",
      "Provenance (mock, live, rule-based, simulation) is always visible next to model output, as a square and a word."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "section": "Colors",
        "name": "Square Means One Thing",
        "body": "A coloured square names a signal state, a participant, a status or a provenance. A square that encodes nothing does not ship, and nothing else in the chrome carries hue."
      },
      {
        "section": "Colors",
        "name": "Signal Colours Mean Signals",
        "body": "Red, amber and green are signal state only; outcomes use `positive`, `warning` and `destructive`."
      },
      {
        "section": "Colors",
        "name": "Identity Pairing",
        "body": "Cyan is North/South and Agent A; violet is East/West and Agent B, in the scene, the timeline, the legends and the charts."
      },
      {
        "section": "Typography",
        "name": "One Family",
        "body": "Onest sets everything; weight, size and case carry hierarchy. There is no monospace face."
      },
      {
        "section": "Typography",
        "name": "Lowercase Chrome",
        "body": "The wordmark and header links are lowercase. Proper names and acronyms inside them keep their case (\"by MAGI\", \"AI\"); body copy uses sentence case."
      },
      {
        "section": "Elevation & Depth",
        "name": "Lamp Is the Only Light",
        "body": "No glow, gradient or coloured shadow on chrome. The one gradient is the Home room falloff, which is the room's own colour fading in, not decoration."
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** draw status, identity and provenance as squares, never dots or pills.",
      "**Do** keep text on the ground; give a surface a slab only when it floats over the scene.",
      "**Do** set every clock, latency and live number with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** pair cyan with North/South and Agent A, violet with East/West and Agent B, everywhere.",
      "**Do** label replay as replay and mock as mock; show null as \"—\" or \"unavailable\", never 0.",
      "**Do** route every colour, scene materials included, through a token in `src/index.css`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** round corners or use a status dot.",
      "**Don't** use signal red, amber or green for success, warning or error.",
      "**Don't** add a hue that encodes nothing, or a second type family.",
      "**Don't** box Home's titles and legends in cards.",
      "**Don't** cover the intersection's centre with a panel or let a panel outweigh the scene.",
      "**Don't** present a replayed moment as the live simulation, or claim the authoritative simulation was rewound."
    ]
  }
}